\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, if still the same Thou art,
\par If all Thy promises are sure,
\par Set up Thy kingdom in my heart,
\par And make me rich, for I am poor:
\par To me be all Thy treasures given,
\par The kingdom of an inward heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou hast pronounced the mourners blest;
\par And lo, for Thee I ever mourn:
\par I cannot: No! I will not rest,
\par Till Thou, my only rest, return;
\par Till Thou, the Prince of Peace, appear,
\par And I receive the Comforter.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Where is the blessedness bestowed
\par On all that hunger after Thee?
\par I hunger now, I thirst for God,
\par See the poor fainting sinner, see,
\par And satisfy with endless peace,
\par And fill me with Thy righteousness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ah, Lord! if Thou art in that sigh,
\par Then hear Thyself within me pray;
\par Hear in my heart Thy Spirit's cry,
\par Mark what my labouring soul would say;
\par Answer the deep unuttered groan,
\par And show that Thou and I are one.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Shine on Thy work, disperse the gloom,
\par Light in Thy light I then shall see;
\par Say to my soul: Thy light is come,
\par Glory divine is risen on thee,
\par Thy warfare's past, thy mourning's o'er,
\par Look up, for Thou shalt  weep no more!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

